      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": {
        "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
        "Label": "CASE REPORT",
        "content": "A 21-year-old woman presenting with low abdominal discomfort, dysmenorrhoea and pelvic mass was misdiagnosed as endometriosis. She had post-traumatic splenic rupture and laparotomy history. RESULTS. Pelvic splenosis was diagnosed at laparotomy. Pelvic mass was removed and the other implants were left."
